error[E0451]: `Reading` can't be a key: `value` is a float
  --> tests/programs/interfaces/eq_key/not_key.la:6:13
  |
6 |     let m = Map { Reading { at: 1, value: 0.5 }: 1 };
  |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  |
  = help: floats compare with `==` but aren't `Key`: `NaN != NaN`, so a float key could never be found again; key by the other parts, or hold the number as an integer (cents, `x.to_bits()`)

error[E0451]: `f64` can't be a key: it is a float
  --> tests/programs/interfaces/eq_key/not_key.la:7:12
  |
7 |     let s: Set<f64> = Set {};
  |            ^^^^^^^^
  |
  = help: floats compare with `==` but aren't `Key`: `NaN != NaN`, so a float key could never be found again; use an integer

For more about E0451, run `lughac explain E0451`.
